  at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

  This file is covered by the PaskalCPP Runtime Exception
  (RUNTIME-EXCEPTION.md).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  mojoal.pcpp - the mojoAL unit: `import mojoal;` gives a PaskalCPP program
  OpenAL 1.1 (3D positional audio: a listener, sources placed around it,
  buffers of sound data) through mojoAL, an OpenAL implementation over
  SDL3's audio. A self-describing vendor module: it owns every path it needs
  and imports sdl3 for SDL's own. The library is libmojoal.a (one per
  target, upstream's mojoal.c built by PaskalCPP-Libs' build-mojoal.cmd),
  linked by @linklibrary: every module of the program shares the one copy.

  The API is OpenAL 1.1 as it ships (AL/al.h, AL/alc.h), called straight
  from PaskalCPP: alcOpenDevice(nil) opens the default playback device,
  alcCreateContext + alcMakeContextCurrent make a context current (the SDL
  audio device is opened here, at the first context), alGenBuffers +
  alBufferData load sound data (AL_FORMAT_MONO8 / MONO16 / STEREO8 /
  STEREO16, and the AL_EXT_FLOAT32 / AL_EXT_32bit_formats formats),
  alGenSources + alSourcei(AL_BUFFER) attach it, alSourcePlay /
  alSourceStop / alGetSourcei(AL_SOURCE_STATE) drive a source, and
  alListener3f / alSource3f(AL_POSITION) place them in 3D. alGetError
  (and alcGetError for the device) report the last error, then clear it.
  mojoAL also offers ALC_EXT_CAPTURE, ALC_EXT_DISCONNECT and
  ALC_EXT_thread_local_context.

  mojoAL starts SDL's audio subsystem itself (SDL_Init(SDL_INIT_AUDIO) in
  alcOpenDevice): a program that uses only OpenAL calls no SDL routine. To
  pick an SDL audio driver, set it before alcOpenDevice, e.g.
  SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DRIVER, "dummy") for a run with no sound
  hardware. Tear down in reverse: alDeleteSources, alDeleteBuffers,
  alcMakeContextCurrent(nil), alcDestroyContext, then alcCloseDevice, which
  returns ALC_FALSE (and closes nothing) while the device still has a
  context or a buffer.

  The library is static: AL_LIBTYPE_STATIC is defined for every includer
  (below), so the AL headers declare plain symbols, never dllimport.
==============================================================================*/

module unit mojoal;

@addincludepath "$P:res/libs/vendor/mojoal/include";

// libmojoal.a is static: every includer must see AL_LIBTYPE_STATIC (no
// dllimport in AL/al.h and AL/alc.h)
@cppdefine "AL_LIBTYPE_STATIC";

// The library of each target; everything it calls is SDL3's (import sdl3)
@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_WINDOWS_GNU
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/mojoal/lib/x86_64-windows-gnu";
@elseif TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/mojoal/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu";
@else
  @message error "mojoal: unsupported target";
@endif

@linklibrary "mojoal";

import sdl3;

// The headers go to this unit's header, so every importer sees OpenAL's API
cpp header;

#include <AL/al.h>
#include <AL/alc.h>

end.
